@node Getting Started
@chapter Getting Started
@cindex getting started
@cindex introduction

@code{beads.el} is a Magit-like Emacs interface for the
@uref{https://github.com/steveyegge/beads, Beads} issue tracker.  It
provides a keyboard-driven, transient-based UI for managing issues,
dependencies, molecules, formulas, agents, and workflows without leaving
Emacs.

@code{beads.el} is a porcelain over the @command{bd} command-line tool:
the UI never parses human-readable output, it always drives
@command{bd --json} and renders the structured result.  Every
@command{bd} command is reachable from Emacs, either through an
auto-generated transient or a curated one.

This chapter installs the package, creates a first issue, explains the
interaction patterns every view shares, and defines the vocabulary the
rest of the manual assumes.  @xref{Issue Workflow}, for the commands that
create, list, view, edit, close, and label issues.

